---
description: Python standards for enterprise codebases
globs: *.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- All Python code must follow PEP 8 and PEP 257
- Functions must have type hints for all parameters and return values
- No magic numbers — use named constants or Enum
- Maximum function length: 40 lines. Refactor beyond that.
- All public APIs must have docstrings with Args, Returns, Raises sections (Google style)
- Use pathlib.Path, not os.path
- Prefer dataclasses or Pydantic models over plain dicts for structured data
